- Immediately call `fchmod(fd, 0600);` to enforce owner-only read/write permissions.  
- Validate `fd != -1` before calling `fchmod()` or proceeding with file operations.  
- Avoid relying on `umask()`; explicitly set file permissions to `0600`.
